@@ -418,3 +418,22 @@ strip beside the housing included, and the guest describes the housing to
 Omarchy's bar through Omarchy's own `display-cutouts.json`, so the bar sits
 beside the camera and windows start below it. See
 [camera notch](camera-notch.md).
+
+## Managed SSH capability 1
+
+A private embedding-manager capability enrolls new UUID roots without changing the public run protocol. The helper validates private `.omarchy-managed-ssh.json` metadata, the matching per-launch provisioning manifest and the exact stored TCP mapping to guest port 22. It sets the internal provisioning-share environment itself; a caller-supplied value is removed. The launch script attaches only that share, read-only, and signals opt-in through `tryomarchy.managed_ssh=1`.
+
+The embedding manager creates an independent client identity and guest host identity per VM. Only the guest host key and authorized public keys are shared. The guest timer waits for normal non-root owner provisioning, preserves the bound owner and host key across boots, and configures the vendor SSH service through a runtime drop-in. Password, interactive and root login are disabled for this opt-in mode. The ordinary authorized-keys file remains supported and untouched.
+
+Guest status carries the VM UUID, launch nonce, provisioning state and owner in an optional schema-1 field. The host validates bounded reports but treats them as advisory. Authenticated SSH must confirm the expected owner and VM/session identity before the manager reports readiness. Initial trust comes from the per-VM provisioning channel, never an unverified network key scan. Changed host identities require explicit recovery.
+
+Managed SSH failures report only a bounded provisioning-stage enum, failure-code enum and optional errno/exit status. Exception messages, command output, paths and key material are excluded. The host validates these optional protocol-1 fields before displaying them.
+
+After mounting the managed 9p share, its inode ownership comes from the Mac. Repeated enrollment verifies the exact mount point, 9p tag and read-only VFS mode under a root-owned guest parent. It does not mistake the Mac-owned mounted root for an ordinary guest-owned directory. Wrong sources, writable mounts and symlinks are refused.
+
+
+### Manager owner setup
+
+The private manager can opt a new UUID root into saved owner setup. Its separate read-only `tryomarchy-managed-setup` share carries a bounded session manifest and temporary password seed. `managed-owner-setup` uses Omarchy's reviewed OEM functions without changing an Omarchy-owned file. It verifies the installed program and helper hashes before sourcing the program without its final `main`, as the upstream desktop CI already does. Answers travel over stdin as NUL-delimited data. Encrypted images and existing owners are refused; a failure reports a fixed code and continues with normal interactive setup.
+
+The manager holds reusable passwords in Keychain. Metadata never contains them. The host removes the staging seed after a matching completion report and on exit; the helper also removes it when the manager is gone. A root-owned completion identity lets a later boot acknowledge a setup that finished while its manager was unavailable. This status is separate from runtime readiness and authenticated SSH readiness. Manual guests get the normal Omarchy owner wizard.
