@@ -182,3 +182,19 @@ hides the guest cursor (Cocoa draws the Mac's) and hides it again whenever a
 window closes, since Omarchy's screensaver shows it as it exits. It also keeps
 the mode in sync with the window through EDID, and applies the pinch and Apple
 keyboard input rules.
+
+## Managed SSH enrollment
+
+An embedding manager can opt an explicitly rooted NAT guest into managed SSH. The private capability version 1 uses a separate read-only `tryomarchy-managed-ssh` share, with the guest host identity and authorized public keys. No client private key crosses into the guest. The package waits for normal owner provisioning, then configures the vendor `sshd.service` for that owner with key authentication and the existing gateway-only firewall rule. It preserves the user's ordinary authorized keys and keeps its own enrollment separate. There is no extra bootstrap account or password.
+
+The protocol-1 guest status report has an optional versioned `managedSSH` field. Its owner/VM/session values are advisory until the manager verifies an authenticated connection against its pinned host identity. Unmanaged Try Omarchy boots keep their existing SSH behavior.
+
+The private manager's optional unattended owner setup uses a separate read-only seed share and an OEM service wrapper. Unknown provisioning scripts, encrypted images, malformed seeds and previously configured owners fall back to normal setup. Package-owned files provide this integration; no Omarchy-owned file is modified.
+
+## Managed owner contracts
+
+Opted-in manager setup selects the official or lean-e4fffc6 contract by its reviewed digest. The helper binds that choice to the verified factory; guest metadata cannot authorize another program set. Root-owned, non-writable regular programs and their source dependencies must match before a private snapshot is sourced. The lean adapter preserves the saved full name and email. A finalization warning preserves pending/setup-user so a retry keeps the same account and SSH remains blocked. Managed failures report a bounded code and stop; only unseeded setup uses the interactive program.
+
+Managed completion is recorded durably before upstream cleanup removes pending. A matching committed owner can retry interrupted cleanup; another identity is refused. Lean finalization executes the canonical hash-checked program, and SSH waits for a configured owner report from the current seeded VM/session.
+
+For a seeded boot the report timer remains active until shutdown. Before reporting configured, the adapter retains a root-private non-secret receipt in /run, bound to the kernel boot ID and a helper-derived report digest in the boot credential. Host completion still immediately removes the password seed, full manifest and launch marker. Later timer invocations revalidate the receipt, committed identity, owner and cleanup against the immutable boot digest; another session or damaged state cannot be acknowledged. A new boot needs fresh host-authorized context. No failed unit is masked or reset.
